module overview
  -- Caravel hosts virtual Nostr relays, sold to tenants on plans and billed monthly.
  -- One binary serves every relay by host, the JSON API, and three embedded Solid apps.

  -- Layers (each depends only on those below; crates/app/tests/layers.rs enforces it)
  ~ db: the Postgres pool, migrations, and `with_tx`, which reruns a transaction Postgres aborts
  ~ adapters: Stripe, Nostr relays, NWC wallets, the robot, DNS, blobs, LiveKit, outbound HTTP
  ~ core: models, then pure domain rules, then queries that read and commands that write,
    then the subsystems that run them against a `Core` (crates/core/tests/layers.rs)
  ~ relay and api above the core read through queries and change state only through subsystems
  ~ app: config from the environment, host dispatch, the embedded web apps, background workers

  -- Entry points
  ~ `main` reads config, connects a request pool and a background pool, builds the `Core`
  ~ `serve` spawns the workers, loads every relay with `Relays::load`, then serves `router`
  ~ `router` sends each request by host: a relay's hosts to `Relays::serve`, the API host to
    the API `router`, the platform host to the dashboards; anything else gets health and TLS ask
  ~ `workers::spawn` schedules billing, domain checks, the session, event and membership sweeps,
    relay erasure, and publishing the robot's identity

  -- Flows
  ~ client event: `session::run` reads a socket -> `RelayInstance::on_event` -> `screen`
    and `admit_write` against the snapshot -> `ingest::store` saves it with what it changes
    -> `broadcast` of it and what the relay published: `fanout` to live subscribers and
    `Pusher::push` to NIP-9a callbacks
  ~ client REQ: `on_req` -> `admit_req` -> subscribe first, then stored events that pass
    `can_any_receive` -> EOSE; later events reach it through `fanout` and `can_deliver`
  ~ NIP-43 join or leave: `ingest::join` / `ingest::leave` -> member list republished by the relay
  ~ NIP-86 call: `nip86::handle` checks a NIP-98 signature over the body -> `management::call`
    -> `apply_access_change` on the instance
  ~ dashboard change: API handler loads the resource, authorizes the actor, calls a subsystem
    (`hosting`, `management`, `memberships`) -> commit -> `Bus::publish` -> `Relays::watch`
    reloads the relay and delivers what it published
  ~ billing: `reconcile_subscriptions` hourly prices activity per tenant, renews, bills overage,
    cuts invoices, collects by NWC or card, reminds by DM, and churns tenants past grace
  ~ memberships: `open_checkout` -> Stripe Connect checkout -> `reconcile_checkout` -> `activate`
    admits the member; `sweep` renews or lapses subscriptions and settles stale checkouts
  ~ sessions: one NIP-98 `POST /session` buys a 30-day bearer token (`sessions::start`),
    stored only as a hash; `Authed` accepts only it
  ~ media: Blossom `upload` -> `media::keep_upload` stores the bytes and records the blob per
    uploader; `delete` removes a pubkey's claim and the bytes once the last owner is gone
  ~ calls: `livekit::token` admits room members by `admit_call`; `livekit::webhook` meters time

  -- Shared state
  ~ `Relays` maps hosts to live `RelayInstance`s behind a lock, swapped on reload
  ~ each instance holds a swappable snapshot of its access, rooms and settings, and its connections
  ~ the `Bus` broadcasts hints after commits; a lagging subscriber reloads everything
  ~ the `Clock` is the only source of time; tests pin it

  -- Web apps (web/src)
  ~ tenant dashboard: relays, plans, billing, and managing a relay over NIP-86, NIP-43 and NIP-29
  ~ admin dashboard under /admin: tenants, relays, invoices, the moderation feed
  ~ member portal on each relay's host: buying, inviting and renewing paid memberships
  ~ `@/shared/lib/api` holds a function per API route; `@/shared/lib/state` the signed-in account
